1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,238
The Iranians are
saying these issues are non-negotiable.

2
00:00:05,538 --> 00:00:07,640
These are demands.

3
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:12,512
We are demanding that
you meet every one of these ten demands.

4
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:17,183
The West is leading
Ukraine down the primrose

5
00:00:17,183 --> 00:00:21,321
path, and the Israelis
are executing a genocide in Gaza.

6
00:00:21,388 --> 00:00:25,058
It's not China's fault
that it wants to be powerful.

7
00:00:25,091 --> 00:00:28,061
So if you get into trouble and you

8
00:00:28,061 --> 00:00:31,064
dial 911, there's nobody at the other

9
00:00:32,132 --> 00:00:34,000
Hi, this is John Mearsheimer.

10
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,040
And what I'd like to talk about
today is the state of the negotiations

11
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:43,043
between the United States and Iran

12
00:00:43,043 --> 00:00:46,613
with regard to ending the ongoing war.

13
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:49,883
And it's quite clear that President Trump

14
00:00:49,883 --> 00:00:52,886
is deeply committed to ending this war.

15
00:00:52,952 --> 00:00:58,191
And he especially is interested
in opening the Strait of Hormuz.

16
00:00:58,391 --> 00:01:03,830
But I would argue that if you look
at what's happened in recent months,

17
00:01:03,997 --> 00:01:08,034
his situation has gone from bad to worse.

18
00:01:08,301 --> 00:01:12,972
And ending the war is going
to be very difficult for him to do.

19
00:01:13,173 --> 00:01:18,578
And the deal
that he is likely to get moving forward

20
00:01:18,611 --> 00:01:23,450
would be worse than any deal
he could have gotten in the past.

21
00:01:23,683 --> 00:01:27,954
But before I get into the nitty gritty
of what's going on today,

22
00:01:28,221 --> 00:01:33,893
I just like to talk a little bit
about sort of the history of negotiations

23
00:01:33,893 --> 00:01:37,030
between Iran and the United States,

24
00:01:37,097 --> 00:01:40,033
going back to the Obama administration.

25
00:01:40,033 --> 00:01:45,772
As I'm sure most viewers remember,
President Obama in 2015

26
00:01:45,772 --> 00:01:49,642
got a nuclear agreement with the Iranians.

27
00:01:49,676 --> 00:01:52,679
It's the famous JCPoA.

28
00:01:52,846 --> 00:01:55,949
And that 2015 agreement

29
00:01:56,049 --> 00:01:59,752
did allow Iran to enrich

30
00:01:59,819 --> 00:02:04,557
uranium, but is unequivocally clear
that there was no way

31
00:02:04,591 --> 00:02:09,529
under that agreement
that Iran could get a nuclear weapon.

32
00:02:09,896 --> 00:02:13,299
President Trump got elected in 2016,

33
00:02:13,299 --> 00:02:17,270
and in 2017,
he moved into the white House.

34
00:02:17,770 --> 00:02:19,739
And remember the agreement?

35
00:02:19,739 --> 00:02:23,176
The JCPoA agreement was in 2015

36
00:02:23,176 --> 00:02:26,179
and the summer of 2018,

37
00:02:26,312 --> 00:02:29,749
President Trump tore up the JCPoA.

38
00:02:30,316 --> 00:02:33,720
He had nothing but contempt for the JCPoA.

39
00:02:33,786 --> 00:02:34,387
He said it was a

40
00:02:34,387 --> 00:02:38,458
terrible nuclear agreement,
and he was going to put maximum pressure.

41
00:02:38,458 --> 00:02:41,594
And I think he met maximum
economic pressure

42
00:02:41,628 --> 00:02:45,064
on the Iranians,
and he was going to get a better deal.

43
00:02:45,098 --> 00:02:46,499
That's what he promised.

44
00:02:46,499 --> 00:02:51,471
And over the course of his first term
in office, he failed to do that.

45
00:02:51,471 --> 00:02:55,175
There was no nuclear agreement
with the Iranians.

46
00:02:55,275 --> 00:02:59,312
And in fact, both the Americans
and the Iranians

47
00:02:59,312 --> 00:03:03,283
began to violate the JCPoA.

48
00:03:03,917 --> 00:03:05,418
Joe Biden came in.

49
00:03:05,418 --> 00:03:08,755
He said he was going to try
and reinstitute the JCPoA.

50
00:03:08,788 --> 00:03:09,689
He failed.

51
00:03:09,689 --> 00:03:13,660
And then, of course,
President Trump comes back to office

52
00:03:13,660 --> 00:03:17,697
in January of 2025.

53
00:03:17,730 --> 00:03:19,599
This is for his second term.

54
00:03:19,599 --> 00:03:23,636
And unsurprisingly,
one of the first things that he turns to

55
00:03:23,770 --> 00:03:27,807
is the Iranian nuclear issue,
because Biden didn't fix it.

56
00:03:27,807 --> 00:03:30,210
And he had promised, when he withdrew

57
00:03:30,210 --> 00:03:34,013
from the JCPoA in 2018
that he'd get a better deal.

58
00:03:34,013 --> 00:03:36,049
But of course, that didn't happen.

59
00:03:36,049 --> 00:03:39,619
So he set out shortly
after he comes into the white House

60
00:03:39,619 --> 00:03:44,157
in January 2025 for the second time
to get a better deal.

61
00:03:44,757 --> 00:03:50,230
And he is negotiating,
or I should say, his administration

62
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:53,233
is negotiating with the Iranians

63
00:03:53,399 --> 00:03:57,737
up through June of 2025.

64
00:03:57,804 --> 00:04:01,608
And while the negotiations are going on,

65
00:04:01,975 --> 00:04:06,779
the Israelis and the Americans
attack the Iranians.

66
00:04:06,813 --> 00:04:11,884
And this is the famous 12 day
war of June 2025.

67
00:04:11,884 --> 00:04:15,388
And this war is aimed at

68
00:04:15,755 --> 00:04:18,491
Iran's nuclear capabilities.

69
00:04:18,491 --> 00:04:22,795
So I think the basic idea here
is that we couldn't get an agreement,

70
00:04:23,529 --> 00:04:26,633
couldn't get a new JCPoA
or anything like that.

71
00:04:26,633 --> 00:04:29,736
So what we'll do is we'll bomb
Iran's nuclear

72
00:04:29,736 --> 00:04:33,206
capabilities,
and that's what we did in the 12 day war.

73
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:36,643
Then if you fast forward up

74
00:04:36,643 --> 00:04:39,912
until February 28th, when

75
00:04:40,046 --> 00:04:43,683
another war, another Israeli American war

76
00:04:43,816 --> 00:04:47,220
was launched against a ram, what you see

77
00:04:47,220 --> 00:04:50,189
is that in the run up to that war.

78
00:04:50,456 --> 00:04:54,193
This is the February 28th war,
just like in the run

79
00:04:54,193 --> 00:04:57,764
up to the June 2025 war.

80
00:04:58,131 --> 00:05:01,934
Negotiations were ongoing
between the Iranians

81
00:05:01,934 --> 00:05:06,272
and the Americans
about how to solve the nuclear issue.

82
00:05:06,439 --> 00:05:11,911
So twice, the Americans
and the Israelis attacked Iran

83
00:05:12,011 --> 00:05:17,517
when nuclear negotiations
were taking place in the war,

84
00:05:17,617 --> 00:05:20,620
obviously broke out on February 28th.

85
00:05:21,154 --> 00:05:26,259
And this raised
a whole host of new issues,

86
00:05:26,259 --> 00:05:29,329
many of which I'll talk about
as we go along here.

87
00:05:29,329 --> 00:05:32,632
Because once the war breaks out,
the nuclear issue

88
00:05:32,632 --> 00:05:35,635
is not the only major issue on the table.

89
00:05:35,868 --> 00:05:38,571
For example,
there's the whole question of

90
00:05:38,571 --> 00:05:42,041
who controls the Strait of Hormuz.

91
00:05:42,408 --> 00:05:46,979
And then there are a whole host of
economic issues that get raised as well.

92
00:05:46,979 --> 00:05:52,885
So it's no longer just the nuclear issue
that's on the table after February 28th.

93
00:05:53,553 --> 00:05:57,190
And there's a bombing campaign
for 40 days,

94
00:05:57,190 --> 00:06:01,594
and that ends on April 8th,
and you have a ceasefire.

95
00:06:01,594 --> 00:06:07,734
And negotiations actually start
between the Iranians and the Americans.

96
00:06:07,734 --> 00:06:13,439
This is when JD Vance goes to Islamabad
and meets with the Iranian negotiators.

97
00:06:13,439 --> 00:06:16,976
So this is the first opportunity
that we have,

98
00:06:17,009 --> 00:06:20,012
the first major opportunity that we have.

99
00:06:20,413 --> 00:06:22,648
The start of the war

100
00:06:22,648 --> 00:06:27,987
to negotiate a deal with the Iranians,
to hopefully settle the nuclear issue,

101
00:06:27,987 --> 00:06:33,159
as well as the other issues
that are now on the table.

102
00:06:33,192 --> 00:06:36,429
But those negotiations go nowhere.

103
00:06:36,629 --> 00:06:41,000
The second big opportunity
we have to negotiate a deal

104
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:46,773
and in a way we do not
a deal, is the memorandum of understanding

105
00:06:46,973 --> 00:06:51,611
that is signed by President Trump
and his Iranian

106
00:06:51,611 --> 00:06:55,148
counterpart on June 17th of this year.

107
00:06:55,148 --> 00:06:58,050
That's June 17th of 2026.

108
00:06:58,050 --> 00:07:03,523
So this is the first evidence
of a concrete agreement

109
00:07:03,523 --> 00:07:07,427
between the Iranians on one side
and the Americans on the other,

110
00:07:07,427 --> 00:07:11,697
and it deals with almost all the issues
that are on the table.

111
00:07:11,697 --> 00:07:15,568
But, of course,
President Trump walks away from that deal.

112
00:07:15,768 --> 00:07:18,438
It effectively falls apart.

113
00:07:18,438 --> 00:07:22,008
And we're now at a point
where the Iranians,

114
00:07:22,208 --> 00:07:25,077
as of Saturday, August 8th,

115
00:07:25,077 --> 00:07:28,314
have put a new proposal on the table

116
00:07:28,481 --> 00:07:32,151
that, in effect, builds
on the memorandum of understanding.

117
00:07:32,151 --> 00:07:35,888
But from an American point of view
is much worse.

118
00:07:36,355 --> 00:07:42,128
So what I want to do here is focus on
the memorandum of understanding

119
00:07:42,128 --> 00:07:47,166
and the deal that Trump effectively
walked away from on June 17th,

120
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:50,803
and show you how much worse

121
00:07:51,170 --> 00:07:54,373
the 8th August proposal, the new proposal

122
00:07:54,373 --> 00:07:58,511
that the Iranians have put on
the table is for the United States.

123
00:07:58,845 --> 00:08:03,082
And one of the key points
that I'm going to make as we go along here

124
00:08:03,082 --> 00:08:08,054
is that we've actually reached the point
where it appears

125
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:11,924
that the nuclear issue,
which was once of paramount

126
00:08:11,958 --> 00:08:17,830
importance, has basically disappeared
from the negotiations,

127
00:08:17,830 --> 00:08:23,536
or it has been minimized to a point
that is really quite shocking.

128
00:08:23,636 --> 00:08:27,640
But let me deal with that later

129
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:33,513
and start by first
just talking about all of the issues

130
00:08:33,513 --> 00:08:37,617
that I think exist
between the Iranians on one side

131
00:08:37,617 --> 00:08:43,256
and the Americans on the other side,
and I think they're basically 11 issues.

132
00:08:43,389 --> 00:08:48,794
And then let me, after laying out
those 11 issues that are on the table,

133
00:08:48,928 --> 00:08:54,800
explain to you how the memorandum
of understanding dealt with those issues.

134
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:57,803
And in switch gears and talk about how

135
00:08:58,237 --> 00:09:03,509
Iran's 8th
August proposal deals with those issues.

136
00:09:03,509 --> 00:09:09,282
And I think you'll see that the Iranians
are really driving a hard bargain.

137
00:09:09,682 --> 00:09:12,718
There's going to be very difficult
for President Trump to accept.

138
00:09:12,718 --> 00:09:16,455
But anyway, before we get there,
what are the key issues here?

139
00:09:17,323 --> 00:09:19,458
Remember I said there are seven issues.

140
00:09:19,458 --> 00:09:22,995
The first issue is just opening
the Strait of Hormuz.

141
00:09:22,995 --> 00:09:26,999
And as I said earlier on, this is
what President Trump really wants to do.

142
00:09:27,033 --> 00:09:28,534
He wants to open the strait.

143
00:09:28,534 --> 00:09:33,239
And when you talk about opening the Strait
of Hormuz, you're basically talking

144
00:09:33,239 --> 00:09:38,411
about doing away
with a Ran's blockade of the strait,

145
00:09:38,411 --> 00:09:42,548
as well as the United States's
blockade of the strait.

146
00:09:42,548 --> 00:09:44,083
So you have to put an end

147
00:09:44,083 --> 00:09:47,987
to these two blockades,
and then you have to allow traffic

148
00:09:48,154 --> 00:09:52,124
to go into
and out of the Strait of Hormuz.

149
00:09:52,592 --> 00:09:56,395
So that's the number one issue,
just opening the strait.

150
00:09:56,429 --> 00:10:02,234
The number two issue is lifting
all sanctions on Iran.

151
00:10:02,401 --> 00:10:03,536
Now be careful here.

152
00:10:03,536 --> 00:10:07,907
You want to note that I'm not talking
about lifting all sanctions on Iran.

153
00:10:07,974 --> 00:10:09,976
There are many sanctions on Iran.

154
00:10:09,976 --> 00:10:13,579
What we're talking about here
is lifting the oil sanctions,

155
00:10:13,579 --> 00:10:17,850
which would allow the Iranians
to sell their oil

156
00:10:18,351 --> 00:10:21,754
on open markets, open global markets.

157
00:10:21,787 --> 00:10:23,889
So that's the second issue.

158
00:10:23,889 --> 00:10:26,592
The third issue is the cease fire,

159
00:10:26,592 --> 00:10:30,830
and I divide the cease fire
into two different issues.

160
00:10:30,896 --> 00:10:34,100
First is the cease fire involving

161
00:10:34,734 --> 00:10:40,339
Israel, the United States and Iran,
the three big players in this conflict.

162
00:10:40,339 --> 00:10:44,043
So there's a cease fire
involving them, in my opinion.

163
00:10:44,043 --> 00:10:48,347
And then there's a cease fire
that deals with

164
00:10:48,547 --> 00:10:51,751
Lebanon, the Houthis,

165
00:10:52,818 --> 00:10:53,819
Hamas, this is

166
00:10:53,819 --> 00:10:57,657
Gaza and now Iraq.

167
00:10:58,357 --> 00:11:00,893
So you want to understand that
when we talk about the cease fire,

168
00:11:00,893 --> 00:11:04,964
I'm discriminating between a cease fire
that involves the United States, Iran

169
00:11:04,964 --> 00:11:06,532
and Israel on one hand.

170
00:11:06,532 --> 00:11:08,934
That's my issue number three, an issue.

171
00:11:08,934 --> 00:11:14,006
Number four is a cease fire that involves
those four different conflicts,

172
00:11:14,006 --> 00:11:17,476
or 1 or 2 of those four different smaller
conflicts.

173
00:11:17,476 --> 00:11:23,349
Again, Gaza, Lebanon,
where Hezbollah is located, Yemen

174
00:11:23,349 --> 00:11:26,352
with the Houthis and the Iranian

175
00:11:26,485 --> 00:11:29,655
allied militias in Iraq.

176
00:11:29,789 --> 00:11:33,125
Okay, so that's the fourth big issue.

177
00:11:33,159 --> 00:11:38,531
Then there's the fifth big issue, which is
who controls the Strait of Hormuz.

178
00:11:38,564 --> 00:11:42,001
Remember, the first issue was just opening
up the Strait of Hormuz.

179
00:11:42,034 --> 00:11:44,937
The fifth issue is who controls it?

180
00:11:44,937 --> 00:11:49,442
The sixth issue related to
that is whether or not

181
00:11:49,508 --> 00:11:53,012
the Iranians can collect tolls

182
00:11:53,112 --> 00:11:56,015
or what are sometimes called fees.

183
00:11:56,015 --> 00:11:59,018
You know, the Iranians are likely to say,
we're not going to collect

184
00:11:59,018 --> 00:12:00,720
tolls, we're going to collect fees.

185
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:03,856
But it's the same thing
for all intents and purposes.

186
00:12:03,889 --> 00:12:07,093
So that is the sixth issue.

187
00:12:07,259 --> 00:12:13,032
The seventh issue
is the US military presence in the region.

188
00:12:13,099 --> 00:12:16,068
And here we're talking
mainly about the Persian Gulf.

189
00:12:16,268 --> 00:12:20,740
Is the United States going to be allowed
to keep its military bases?

190
00:12:20,773 --> 00:12:24,276
It's force structure in the Persian Gulf.

191
00:12:24,343 --> 00:12:28,247
And everybody knows before February 28th,

192
00:12:28,247 --> 00:12:33,085
we had a robust force structure,
a robust set of bases in the region.

193
00:12:33,085 --> 00:12:36,856
And the issue here, issue number seven, is

194
00:12:36,856 --> 00:12:40,192
what's going to happen
to the American military presence.

195
00:12:40,326 --> 00:12:43,829
Then we come to issues
eight, nine and ten,

196
00:12:43,896 --> 00:12:48,067
which are the big three economic issues
and all very important.

197
00:12:49,335 --> 00:12:51,670
The eighth issue deals with sanctions.

198
00:12:51,670 --> 00:12:55,407
And this is where we're talking about
all sanctions

199
00:12:55,441 --> 00:12:59,078
lifting sanctions on Iran, period.

200
00:12:59,211 --> 00:13:03,015
Remember earlier on when I talked
about the second issue, they'd have to

201
00:13:03,048 --> 00:13:06,619
that had to do with just lifting
the oil sanctions here

202
00:13:06,919 --> 00:13:09,889
with issue number eight,

203
00:13:09,889 --> 00:13:13,292
we're talking about lifting all sanctions.

204
00:13:13,526 --> 00:13:19,932
Issue number nine is unfreezing
Iranian assets.

205
00:13:20,166 --> 00:13:23,435
100 plus billion dollars of Iranian

206
00:13:23,435 --> 00:13:26,772
assets are frozen outside of Iran.

207
00:13:26,772 --> 00:13:31,844
And the Iranians obviously
want those frozen assets unfrozen.

208
00:13:31,877 --> 00:13:33,879
Okay, so that's the ninth issue.

209
00:13:33,879 --> 00:13:37,850
And the 10th issue is paying reparations.

210
00:13:37,883 --> 00:13:42,054
And the number that's
usually thrown around is $300 billion.

211
00:13:42,154 --> 00:13:46,091
The idea is that someone
who knows for sure

212
00:13:46,091 --> 00:13:50,095
which countries would be involved here,
but the Iranians will get roughly

213
00:13:50,095 --> 00:13:55,134
$300 billion in reparations
if this is ever agreed to.

214
00:13:55,167 --> 00:13:57,169
But this is the 10th issue.

215
00:13:57,169 --> 00:13:59,038
And again, I want to be very clear here.

216
00:13:59,038 --> 00:14:04,376
The eighth, ninth and 10th issues are
what I call the big three economic issues.

217
00:14:04,510 --> 00:14:07,680
And that's, you know, reparations,

218
00:14:08,047 --> 00:14:11,250
frozen assets and sanctions,
all sanctions.

219
00:14:11,283 --> 00:14:14,286
Okay. Then there's the 11th issue.

220
00:14:14,386 --> 00:14:18,157
And I don't want to argue
that this is the least important issue.

221
00:14:18,157 --> 00:14:20,893
But the 11th issue is the nuclear issue.

222
00:14:20,893 --> 00:14:24,163
And here we're talking
about the question of nuclear enrichment.

223
00:14:24,163 --> 00:14:25,698
That's the issue.

224
00:14:25,698 --> 00:14:28,701
And when we talk about nuclear enrichment

225
00:14:29,134 --> 00:14:31,670
you want to remember
there are two dimensions to that.

226
00:14:31,670 --> 00:14:35,507
One is or the Iranians going to be allowed

227
00:14:35,975 --> 00:14:40,646
to have a nuclear enrichment capability.

228
00:14:40,646 --> 00:14:41,714
That's one issue.

229
00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:45,150
And then number two is
what's going to be done

230
00:14:45,150 --> 00:14:50,356
with all that enriched uranium
that the Iranians have.

231
00:14:51,090 --> 00:14:57,162
You want to remember, they have a great
deal of Iranian that's enriched up to 60%.

232
00:14:57,162 --> 00:15:02,801
And it's quite easy to take uranium
that's enriched up to 60%

233
00:15:02,801 --> 00:15:07,439
and enrich it up to 90%,
which is weapons grade material.

234
00:15:07,573 --> 00:15:12,111
So again, when we talk about
the nuclear issue, question number one is

235
00:15:12,111 --> 00:15:15,214
can they keep their nuclear enrichment
capability.

236
00:15:15,214 --> 00:15:19,285
And number two is what do you do
with all that enriched uranium.

237
00:15:19,318 --> 00:15:19,752
Okay.

238
00:15:19,752 --> 00:15:23,289
So those are the big Levin issues.

239
00:15:23,522 --> 00:15:26,525
And you could see
just how complicated all of this is

240
00:15:26,525 --> 00:15:29,895
when you take into account
those 11 issues.

241
00:15:30,629 --> 00:15:32,998
Now what I want to do

242
00:15:32,998 --> 00:15:38,771
is I want to talk about my understanding
of how the Memorandum of Understanding

243
00:15:38,804 --> 00:15:42,908
of 17th June dealt with all those issues.

244
00:15:43,042 --> 00:15:47,246
And then I want to talk about
how the Iranians 8th

245
00:15:47,246 --> 00:15:51,617
August proposal deals with those issues,

246
00:15:51,617 --> 00:15:56,288
and look at the difference
in terms of what's happening here.

247
00:15:56,322 --> 00:15:57,189
Okay.

248
00:15:57,189 --> 00:16:00,559
Let's go to the 17th June memorandum

249
00:16:00,559 --> 00:16:03,796
of understanding upfront.

250
00:16:04,330 --> 00:16:08,167
There were four issues
that were basically settled.

251
00:16:08,167 --> 00:16:13,739
And once those four issues were settled,
the negotiations would set in.

252
00:16:13,739 --> 00:16:19,645
And then you would deal through
negotiations with all these other issues.

253
00:16:20,012 --> 00:16:25,084
Now, what issues were settled up front
in the Memorandum of understanding?

254
00:16:25,150 --> 00:16:28,487
First of all, is opening
the straight right.

255
00:16:28,520 --> 00:16:33,058
The memorandum of understanding started by
saying we're going to open the strait.

256
00:16:33,092 --> 00:16:34,560
Number one.

257
00:16:34,560 --> 00:16:37,396
Number two, we're going to lift

258
00:16:37,396 --> 00:16:40,566
sanctions
just, well, sanctions on the Iranians

259
00:16:40,566 --> 00:16:43,569
so they can sell their all in open
markets.

260
00:16:43,936 --> 00:16:47,373
Number three,
we're going to have a cease fire

261
00:16:47,406 --> 00:16:50,909
between Iran,
Israel and the United States.

262
00:16:52,211 --> 00:16:54,613
And then fourth,

263
00:16:54,613 --> 00:16:58,417
there was going to be a cease fire
involving southern Lebanon,

264
00:16:59,251 --> 00:17:02,888
not involving the Houthis,

265
00:17:02,921 --> 00:17:07,559
not involving Hamas, and not involving
Iraq, just southern Lebanon.

266
00:17:07,559 --> 00:17:11,730
In fact, that was article
one of the memorandum of understanding.

267
00:17:11,830 --> 00:17:15,067
Okay, so you see,
there was agreement on four issues.

268
00:17:15,134 --> 00:17:19,071
The first just had to do with opening
the strait, doing away with the blockade.

269
00:17:19,138 --> 00:17:24,276
The second said that the Iranians
could sell their all on global markets.

270
00:17:24,343 --> 00:17:28,113
And then the third and fourth
have to do with the ceasefires.

271
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:31,683
Okay. Now,
what about all the other issues?

272
00:17:31,750 --> 00:17:37,089
For example, the whole question

273
00:17:37,122 --> 00:17:41,693
of who controls the strait,
the whole question of tolls.

274
00:17:42,127 --> 00:17:46,098
The whole question of the US
military presence,

275
00:17:46,365 --> 00:17:49,401
then the big three economic issues.

276
00:17:49,401 --> 00:17:54,339
This is, of course, 
eliminating all sanctions,

277
00:17:54,873 --> 00:17:59,244
reparations and the frozen assets.

278
00:17:59,244 --> 00:18:02,414
And then very importantly,
the nuclear issue.

279
00:18:02,748 --> 00:18:07,119
All these issues were to be negotiated

280
00:18:07,119 --> 00:18:12,191
in a 60 day period that ensued

281
00:18:12,257 --> 00:18:17,629
after you got a cease fire in place
and after the strait was opened.

282
00:18:19,965 --> 00:18:22,134
What's really going on here,

283
00:18:22,134 --> 00:18:26,839
I think,
is that in the negotiating process,

284
00:18:27,539 --> 00:18:31,977
the key issues were the economic issues
and the nuclear issue, the question

285
00:18:32,010 --> 00:18:36,815
of control of the strait,
whether the Iranians can collect tolls,

286
00:18:36,815 --> 00:18:40,119
and the question of the US
military presence in the region.

287
00:18:40,119 --> 00:18:45,224
I don't think those were terribly
important issues to be negotiated.

288
00:18:45,257 --> 00:18:47,292
I think it was quite clear
that the Iranians

289
00:18:47,292 --> 00:18:49,361
were going to control
the Strait of Hormuz.

290
00:18:49,361 --> 00:18:52,364
I think it's quite clear that they could

291
00:18:52,898 --> 00:18:54,366
collect tolls.

292
00:18:54,366 --> 00:18:57,769
And I think the United States
is not going to be able

293
00:18:57,769 --> 00:19:01,039
to go back into the Gulf region
in any meaningful way,

294
00:19:01,073 --> 00:19:05,010
given what's happened
since the war started on February 28th.

295
00:19:05,043 --> 00:19:09,014
I think what was going to happen
in the memorandum of understanding

296
00:19:09,014 --> 00:19:14,052
is that the United States was going to use
those three economic levers,

297
00:19:14,319 --> 00:19:20,526
removing all sanctions, unfreezing assets,
and that's all assets.

298
00:19:20,526 --> 00:19:24,329
And the reparations issue

299
00:19:24,329 --> 00:19:27,599
to get a good deal

300
00:19:27,599 --> 00:19:32,604
with the Iranians on the nuclear issue,
I think to the extent

301
00:19:32,604 --> 00:19:39,678
that the United States had leverage over
the Iranians vis a vis

302
00:19:39,711 --> 00:19:45,817
the memorandum of understanding,
it came with those economic benefits

303
00:19:45,918 --> 00:19:51,089
that the United States
could see to the Iranians

304
00:19:51,089 --> 00:19:55,027
if they were cooperative
on the nuclear issue.

305
00:19:55,327 --> 00:19:57,529
That was the memorandum of understanding.

306
00:19:57,529 --> 00:19:59,164
Of course, it was the Trump

307
00:19:59,164 --> 00:20:03,035
administration that walked away
from the memorandum of understanding.

308
00:20:03,068 --> 00:20:07,739
Very important to understand
that the United States

309
00:20:07,739 --> 00:20:12,844
was unhappy with that memorandum,
and it thought that it could play hardball

310
00:20:12,844 --> 00:20:16,648
with the Iranians
and hopefully get an even better deal,

311
00:20:16,682 --> 00:20:20,619
because the United States never liked
the memorandum of understanding,

312
00:20:20,619 --> 00:20:25,857
because it definitely was a victory
for the Iranians.

313
00:20:26,058 --> 00:20:28,961
I like to refer to it
as a surrender document,

314
00:20:28,961 --> 00:20:32,731
which I think it was, but the United
States thought it could get a better deal.

315
00:20:32,731 --> 00:20:36,735
And in the course of the month of July,

316
00:20:36,768 --> 00:20:41,807
from roughly July 7th to July 31st,
you had this tit for tat campaign

317
00:20:41,807 --> 00:20:45,877
that took place between the Iranians
and the Americans.

318
00:20:45,877 --> 00:20:50,515
And when it finally ended,

319
00:20:50,515 --> 00:20:54,987
it was quite clear that the United States
did not have any coercive leverage,

320
00:20:55,254 --> 00:20:59,858
that it could prove that could improve
the memorandum of understanding.

321
00:20:59,891 --> 00:21:03,729
And if anything, what became clear
after the tit for tat

322
00:21:03,729 --> 00:21:09,201
strategy ended was that
the Iranians were in the driver's seat.

323
00:21:09,201 --> 00:21:12,537
And once the tit for tat

324
00:21:12,537 --> 00:21:16,842
strategy ended, all sorts of articles
began to appear that said

325
00:21:16,842 --> 00:21:20,679
that the American inventory
of sophisticated weapon weaponry

326
00:21:20,712 --> 00:21:24,750
had basically run dry,
implying that the United States

327
00:21:25,350 --> 00:21:28,387
was in no position to restart the war.

328
00:21:28,887 --> 00:21:31,657
And I think that this point, the Iranians

329
00:21:31,657 --> 00:21:35,360
really understood
that they were in the driver's seat.

330
00:21:35,494 --> 00:21:38,597
So what happens on 8th

331
00:21:38,597 --> 00:21:42,834
August is that the Iranians put forward

332
00:21:42,834 --> 00:21:46,571
a new proposal,
which is actually quite remarkable.

333
00:21:46,638 --> 00:21:53,679
What they say in that proposal
is that every one of the issues,

334
00:21:53,712 --> 00:21:59,885
except the nuclear issue
has to be settled upfront,

335
00:22:00,218 --> 00:22:05,657
which is another way of saying
the United States has to concede on

336
00:22:05,657 --> 00:22:11,096
every one of the ten issues
that I described before.

337
00:22:12,497 --> 00:22:15,267
What exactly does this mean?

338
00:22:15,267 --> 00:22:18,136
The strait has to be opened.

339
00:22:18,136 --> 00:22:21,673
We're not only talking now
about lifting of sanctions,

340
00:22:21,673 --> 00:22:24,643
we're talking about lifting all sanctions.

341
00:22:24,643 --> 00:22:27,579
With regard to the cease fire,

342
00:22:27,579 --> 00:22:31,750
the Iranians are now demanding
a cease fire, not just in Lebanon,

343
00:22:31,750 --> 00:22:36,755
but a cease fire in Gaza and in the West

344
00:22:36,755 --> 00:22:39,758
Bank, a cease fire in Iraq

345
00:22:39,758 --> 00:22:45,430
and a cease fire with the Houthis
and the civil war

346
00:22:45,497 --> 00:22:49,134
that is now taking place in Yemen.

347
00:22:49,334 --> 00:22:54,973
Furthermore, the Who these
I mean, the Iranians make it clear

348
00:22:55,006 --> 00:23:00,245
that they're going to control the Strait
of Hormuz, that they're going to collect

349
00:23:00,278 --> 00:23:05,817
tolls in the Strait of Hormuz,
that the American military presence

350
00:23:05,817 --> 00:23:10,255
in the Persian Gulf
has to disappear completely.

351
00:23:10,422 --> 00:23:13,458
And in addition to all sanctions

352
00:23:13,458 --> 00:23:17,129
being lifted, 
all assets have to be unfrozen.

353
00:23:17,129 --> 00:23:22,834
And the United States, either by itself
or with help from its friends

354
00:23:22,834 --> 00:23:28,373
in the Persian Gulf, has to pay
$300 billion in reparations.

355
00:23:28,407 --> 00:23:30,108
This is really stunning.

356
00:23:30,108 --> 00:23:32,611
You want to understand
what's going on here?

357
00:23:32,611 --> 00:23:37,349
The Iranians are saying
these issues are non-negotiable.

358
00:23:37,649 --> 00:23:39,751
These are demands.

359
00:23:39,751 --> 00:23:44,790
We are demanding that
you meet every one of these ten demands.

360
00:23:46,191 --> 00:23:49,561
So different
than the memorandum of understanding.

361
00:23:49,761 --> 00:23:54,900
Furthermore,
there's no discussion of the nuclear issue

362
00:23:55,400 --> 00:23:59,404
and the problem
that the United States faces here

363
00:23:59,404 --> 00:24:04,109
is that if it pushes forward
on the nuclear issue,

364
00:24:04,643 --> 00:24:09,681
and it says to the Iranians,
that will cave on those ten demands.

365
00:24:09,881 --> 00:24:15,454
But what we want is a bargaining situation
on the nuclear issue.

366
00:24:15,587 --> 00:24:20,892
The fact is, we have no leverage anymore
because our leverage was built

367
00:24:20,892 --> 00:24:26,698
in to those economic goodies
that we could give the Iranians.

368
00:24:26,731 --> 00:24:29,801
In other words, reparations, sanctions,

369
00:24:29,801 --> 00:24:33,071
removal and unfreezing the assets.

370
00:24:33,071 --> 00:24:34,539
They're all gone now.

371
00:24:34,539 --> 00:24:37,509
We have no more bargaining leverage.

372
00:24:38,210 --> 00:24:42,214
So the nuclear issue is sitting out there
by itself.

373
00:24:42,214 --> 00:24:45,150
It's hard to see how it gets settled.

374
00:24:45,150 --> 00:24:48,153
And on top of that,

375
00:24:48,253 --> 00:24:52,123
it's important
to understand that the Iranians now

376
00:24:52,257 --> 00:24:56,394
have a tremendous incentive
to get nuclear weapons afterwards.

377
00:24:56,394 --> 00:24:58,830
Happened since February 28th.

378
00:24:58,830 --> 00:25:02,834
In fact, I think you could go back
to the June war of 2025

379
00:25:02,834 --> 00:25:06,338
and say that
if you look at what happened in June 2025

380
00:25:06,338 --> 00:25:09,307
and you look at what's happened
since February 28th,

381
00:25:09,374 --> 00:25:13,778
the Iranians would be fools
not to acquire nuclear weapons.

382
00:25:13,778 --> 00:25:16,848
And furthermore,
there's all sorts of people say the people

383
00:25:16,848 --> 00:25:22,087
who are now in charge in Iran
are more inclined to want nuclear weapons,

384
00:25:22,120 --> 00:25:25,690
given what they've said in the past,
then their predecessors were.

385
00:25:27,259 --> 00:25:30,729
So if you think about what's happened
here,

386
00:25:31,096 --> 00:25:34,099
going back to the JCPoA

387
00:25:34,499 --> 00:25:37,769
and going back to what happened

388
00:25:37,869 --> 00:25:42,007
before the February 28th war is very clear

389
00:25:42,107 --> 00:25:47,779
that during that lengthy period,
the nuclear issue was the key issue.

390
00:25:48,046 --> 00:25:52,250
But what's happened here
is that we've now reached the point

391
00:25:52,250 --> 00:25:57,155
with the 8th August proposal
that the Iranians have put on the table.

392
00:25:57,289 --> 00:25:59,057
Were the nuclear issue.

393
00:25:59,057 --> 00:26:02,193
It may be too strong to say
that it's been sidelined,

394
00:26:02,227 --> 00:26:05,230
but it is now an issue

395
00:26:05,230 --> 00:26:08,099
that is going to be

396
00:26:08,099 --> 00:26:11,169
incredibly difficult for the United States

397
00:26:11,169 --> 00:26:14,172
and Israel to resolve

398
00:26:14,339 --> 00:26:18,777
in ways that we find satisfactory.

399
00:26:18,777 --> 00:26:23,348
And again,
this is because we have remarkably

400
00:26:23,348 --> 00:26:26,351
little bargaining leverage.

401
00:26:27,118 --> 00:26:30,989
What's happened here
is that as time has gone by,

402
00:26:31,089 --> 00:26:35,694
our bargaining leverage has decreased
in significant ways.

403
00:26:36,194 --> 00:26:40,231
Before the June war,
we were in a very good position

404
00:26:40,231 --> 00:26:44,035
to get a decent,
if not good deal from the Iranians.

405
00:26:44,135 --> 00:26:46,538
That's before the June 2025 war.

406
00:26:46,538 --> 00:26:51,509
The same thing was true before February
28th, and I would argue

407
00:26:51,576 --> 00:26:55,880
that we were in a better position
to get a deal after April 8th

408
00:26:57,148 --> 00:26:58,917
than we are today.

409
00:26:58,917 --> 00:27:02,120
And as I've tried to make clear here
today,

410
00:27:02,921 --> 00:27:07,158
the memorandum of understanding
was much preferable to the deal that

411
00:27:07,192 --> 00:27:10,195
Iranians have now been put on the table.

412
00:27:11,229 --> 00:27:14,599
So I think the question
you have to ask yourself is,

413
00:27:14,599 --> 00:27:18,203
what is President Trump
going to do at this point in time?

414
00:27:18,570 --> 00:27:24,042
Can he accept this deal
that the Iranians have put forth?

415
00:27:24,075 --> 00:27:26,044
It's really hard to imagine

416
00:27:26,044 --> 00:27:30,915
it would be a humiliating defeat feat
for the United States.

417
00:27:30,949 --> 00:27:35,320
It would be a humiliating defeat
for President Trump.

418
00:27:35,887 --> 00:27:38,490
But then the question is,

419
00:27:38,490 --> 00:27:42,794
what can he do
if he doesn't want to accept the deal?

420
00:27:42,794 --> 00:27:46,965
And at the same time,
he's desperate to open the strait.

421
00:27:47,666 --> 00:27:50,669
He has no military option here.

422
00:27:51,036 --> 00:27:56,274
As I've said before on my YouTube
channel, there is no military option.

423
00:27:57,809 --> 00:27:58,176
You know,

424
00:27:58,176 --> 00:28:01,179
you hear a lot today about the fact that

425
00:28:01,846 --> 00:28:04,949
our precious munitions stockpile

426
00:28:04,949 --> 00:28:09,320
has been badly depleted, and that's why
we don't have a military option.

427
00:28:09,554 --> 00:28:14,526
I would make the argument
that even when that precious

428
00:28:14,959 --> 00:28:19,130
stockpile of weapons was available

429
00:28:19,164 --> 00:28:24,135
and when we were using it,
it didn't produce a victory for us.

430
00:28:24,169 --> 00:28:28,339
We had the 40 Day War and we lost.

431
00:28:28,673 --> 00:28:31,443
We had a tit for tat conflict

432
00:28:31,443 --> 00:28:34,446
throughout the month of July,
and it didn't work.

433
00:28:35,013 --> 00:28:41,519
The problem that we face here is not
a shortage of the right kinds of weapons.

434
00:28:41,553 --> 00:28:45,557
The problem that we face
is that there's no way, using America's

435
00:28:45,557 --> 00:28:49,194
military posture,
that we can defeat the Iranians.

436
00:28:49,227 --> 00:28:52,363
We don't have any coercive leverage.

437
00:28:52,397 --> 00:28:56,201
So it's hard to see what president can

438
00:28:56,234 --> 00:29:00,071
President Trump can do other than accept

439
00:29:01,439 --> 00:29:03,374
the deal that

440
00:29:03,374 --> 00:29:08,179
the Iranians have put on the table on
August 8th.

441
00:29:08,279 --> 00:29:11,249
But if he does accept

442
00:29:11,249 --> 00:29:14,919
that deal,
it will be a humiliating defeat.

443
00:29:14,919 --> 00:29:19,257
It will be a devastating defeat for him
and for the United States.

444
00:29:19,257 --> 00:29:23,795
And very importantly,
it will leave the nuclear issue

445
00:29:23,828 --> 00:29:28,700
hanging and it will leave us in a position
where we have

446
00:29:28,933 --> 00:29:32,036
hardly any leverage to deal

447
00:29:32,036 --> 00:29:35,039
with that terribly important issue.

448
00:29:36,007 --> 00:29:38,643
On that sad note, I will conclude,

449
00:29:38,643 --> 00:29:43,281
and I want to thank everyone
for listening to this video,

450
00:29:43,281 --> 00:29:47,485
and I look forward to my next
video with you.

451
00:29:47,485 --> 00:29:48,653
Thank you.

